      <div><font size=3D"2">OpenVPN 3 Linux v25 (Stable release)</font></di=
v>
      <div><font size=3D"2"><br>
        </font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">The v25 release provides three new features
          and several enhancements</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">since the previous release.</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2"><br>
        </font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">Please notice the deprecation of
          openvpn3-autoload.</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2"><br>
        </font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">* Feature: Live route updates (PUSH_UPDATE)
          support</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 When connecting to OpenVPN servers capab=
le
          of pushing new</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 network configurations, such as new netw=
ork
          routes, the</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 OpenVPN 3 Linux client will now update t=
he
          current VPN</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 network setup, including DNS, and replac=
e it
          with the previous</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 configuration without triggering a recon=
nect
          to the server.</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2"><br>
        </font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">* Feature: Automatic restart of VPN client
          processes disappearing</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 When configured, the OpenVPN 3 Linux Ses=
sion
          Manager service</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 will now detect if a VPN process
          unexpectedly disappears and</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 will attempt to restart it automatically=
.</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 See the --automatic-restart option in the
          openvpn3 config-manage</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 man page for further details. =C2=A0This=
 feature
          is disabled by</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 default.</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2"><br>
        </font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">* Feature: AWS VPC integration can now use
          named routing tables</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 When the "route-table-name" setting is
          configured in the</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 OpenVPN 3 AWS Integration add-on, this
          add-on will perform a</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 lookup for this AWS VPC routing table and
          apply the routes here.</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 If this table is not to be found, the ad=
d-on
          will create it</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">=C2=A0 on-the-fly as needed.</font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2"><br>
        </font></div>
      <div><font size=3D"2">* FEATURE DEPRECATION: openvpn3-autoload</font>=
</div>
